\title{Onto / surjective}
\date{2026-03-10T10:54:50Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Definition}
\p{A function #{f : A \to B} is \em{onto} (\em{surjective}, a \em{surjection}) if “every element of #{B} is covered”, that is, ##{\forall b \in B \st \exists a \in A \st f(a) = b.} Put another way, #{f} is onto if the [range](009R) of #{f} is the same as the [codomain](009P).}


